  "statements": [
    {
      "type": "Precautions re: All Other",
      "notes": "As a reminder, discuss the supplements and medications you take with your health care providers."
    },
    {
      "type": "FDA Statement of Identity",
      "notes": "PRODUCT BENEFITS: Melatonin is a natural lipophilic hormone secreted by the Pineal Gland in the brain, and is classified as an Indoleamine."
    },
    {
      "type": "General Statements: All Other Content",
      "notes": "Closely involved in the natural sleep cycle, Melatonin can help support restful sleep patterns.*"
    },
    {
      "type": "General Statements: All Other Content",
      "notes": "Melatonin may be appropriate for people experiencing occasional sleeplessness, those with jet lag or those wanting to promote sound, quality sleep.*"
    },
    {
      "type": "General Statements: All Other Content",
      "notes": "These positive effects are most likely mediated through Melatonin's involvement with membrane-bound receptors located in the Suprachiasmatic Nucleas, the Pars Tuberalis, and other brain regions.*"
    },
    {
      "type": "Suggested/Recommended/Usage/Directions",
      "notes": "Directions: For adults, take one (1) tablet at bedtime as Melatonin may produce drowsiness, or follow the advice of your health care professional."
    },
    {
      "type": "FDA Disclaimer Statement",
      "notes": "*These statements have not been evaluated by the FDA. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure or prevent any disease."
    },
    {
